  "gate_should_answer": false,
  "pre_gate_answer": "# Briefing: TMRS General Investment Consultant Annual Fee\n\n## Conclusion\n**The current annual fee TMRS pays its incumbent general investment consultant is not disclosed in the provided evidence.**  \nBased on the cited materials, the amount **cannot be determined**.\n\n## Evidence Reviewed\n- **Document:** TMRS Request for Proposal for Non-Discretionary General Investment Consulting Services\n- **Date:** February 3, 2022\n\n## Key Findings\n- The document is an **RFP soliciting proposals** for investment consulting services.\n- In **Section VIII, “Fee Proposal,”** respondents are asked to provide a **“total all-inclusive annual fee.”**\n- TMRS also notes that some **additional services** may be priced separately, including:\n  - **Asset/Liability studies**\n  - **Practice & Performance report** under Texas Statute §802.109\n- The draft agreement leaves compensation **blank**, stating only:\n  - **“Consultant’s annual Fee for performance of the services shall be ________ ($______).”**\n\n## What the Evidence Does Not Provide\n- **No dollar amount** for the incumbent consultant’s current annual fee\n- **No identification** of the incumbent consultant in the fee section\n- **No executed contract, award notice, or board approval document** showing final compensation\n\n## Bottom Line\nThe provided TMRS materials **do not state the current annual fee** paid to the incumbent general investment consultant. The query **cannot be answered from this evidence alone**.",
